Fix: the base card was 12px while the widget cards beside it were 24px

DESIGN.md's own C7 says radius and elevation encode containment: the
containing card is the largest radius on the page (--ns-radius-3xl) with the
diffuse ambient shadow, and a panel inside it steps down (--ns-radius-xl).

surface-styles.css gave .ns-card and .ns-panel one shared rule at --ns-radius-xl
with no shadow. WidgetCard set its own 24px + ambient on top, so the app had
two card grammars on the same page: the run console renders a bare Card
summary directly above WidgetCard progress and comparison cards, at half the
radius and no elevation.

Split the rule. The card takes the reference's 24px and the ambient shadow;
the panel steps down to 12px and drops the shadow, because at the card's own
radius and elevation it reads as a second card competing with its host.

Also steps .ns-card__title up one token (sm -> base). It was 14px, exactly the
size of the .ns-card__description under it, so the pair read as one paragraph
and the title never announced what the card was — the vision critique's
"the titles have no presence" (§5).
EOF
