Fix: give the run summary the widget grammar the critique asked for

The vision critique named this file as the page where the five-band grammar
did not exist (§2, §5): "a generic metadata card and a separate 4-box
StatsGrid ... a collection of disconnected rectangular tiles rather than
cohesive dashboard widget cards", with four stats of identical visual weight
and "no large hero number that commands the page".

It still read exactly that way, and now sat directly above the run-progress
and run-comparison widgets this branch added — one page, two card grammars.

The run's own card is now the answer: period as the heading, computed total as
the hero, and the three counts as hairline footer columns instead of four
tiles of equal weight (C1, C2, C5).

- Absence is carried through: an unmeasured console leaves every column null,
  so the hero and all three columns show the em dash rather than $0.00 (M1).
- The failed-count warning only appears when something failed; the console-
  unavailable warning only when the projection did not answer. Both were
  previously either missing or unconditional.
- The heading is an h1, not WidgetCard.Title: it is the route's only top-level
  heading and the title component renders a p. It carries the band's own title
  class so it still reads as the title.
- The not-found / denied / unavailable states stay bare Cards. A card with no
  single answer to give has no hero band (C2).

Rendered in every state to confirm: all four bands present, h1 preserved,
$1,240,500.00 as the hero, three columns, em dashes throughout when the
console is absent.
EOF
