+**Correction (pass 9): the disagreement is one trailing comma, not whitespace.**
+Pass 8 recorded the build's re-dirtied diff as "whitespace-only". It is not.
+Stripping every whitespace character from both forms leaves a **one-character**
+difference in all five files, and it is always the same character:
+
+```diff
+-  .withRouteContract({ $route: …, pathSchema: z.object({ id: z.string() }), })
++  .withRouteContract({ $route: …, pathSchema: z.object({ id: z.string() }) })
+```
+
+`deno fmt` breaks the call across lines *because* it is too wide, and a broken
+object literal gets a trailing comma. The generator emits the same call on one
+line with no trailing comma. So the two writers disagree about punctuation, and
+fmt can never be idempotent against a build: whichever side wins, the other
+rewrites it. No behavioural difference — a trailing comma in an object literal
+changes nothing at runtime — but "whitespace-only" would send the next session
+looking for a line-width knob when the real fix is a trailing comma the
+generator has to emit (or stop emitting).
+
