+## Two card radii on one page — the base `.ns-card` never took C7
+
+**Found 2026-09-04 (design steer #2, pass 9).** `DESIGN.md`'s C7 states that
+radius encodes containment: the containing card is `--ns-radius-3xl` (24px) and
+carries `--ns-shadow-ambient`, a panel inside it steps down to
+`--ns-radius-xl`, and every control inside those is a full pill.
+
+`assets/ui/surface-styles.css` gave `.ns-card` **and** `.ns-panel` one shared
+rule at `--ns-radius-xl` with no shadow. `WidgetCard` set 24px plus the ambient
+shadow on top of it, so the app grew two card grammars: the run console
+rendered a bare `Card` summary at 12px with no elevation directly above a
+`WidgetCard` progress gauge and a `WidgetCard` comparison chart, both at 24px.
+The critique's Ranked Item 3 ("update `.ns-card` radius to 24px") had been
+reported closed because the *widget* card was.
+
+`.ns-card__title` was `--ns-text-sm` — 14px, the exact size of
+`.ns-card__description` underneath it — which is the critique's §5 "the titles
+have no presence".
+
+Split the rule (`25a9a12`): the card takes 24px and the ambient shadow, the
+panel steps down to 12px and drops the shadow, and the title steps up one
+token. Nothing nests a card inside a card in this tree (checked), so raising
+the outer radius cannot collide; `stats-grid` and `data-table` are `Card`s and
+now match the widgets they sit beside.
+
+## The scaffold sweep renamed the fiction, it did not remove it
+
+**Found 2026-09-04 (design steer #2, pass 9).** Rule 8 was reported closed
+after `api-gateway`, `eu-west` and `v2.4.1` were deleted from the gallery
+(`ba37797`). It was not closed. Those were the words someone had already
+thought to name; the scaffold was still shipping behind words nobody had — a
+"Build pipeline" card in the billing gallery, a "Deployment region" select
+whose options were billing periods, "P95 latency / 184ms / All regions" as the
+`StatsGrid` demo, `Enable build cache`, `Maintenance mode`, `Service name`,
+`API key`, `Upload`, `Migration`, and three design-gallery page titles branded
+"NetScript design system" (one describing "the scaffolded @netscript/fresh-ui
+theme"). The landing page's stat row measured the app: "UI source: app-owned",
+"Theme: paper & ink", "see RECORD.md".
+
+A denylist only catches what someone already thought to name, which is why
+this survived three passes under a green R8. The terms are now in the test
+alongside two patterns for the *shape* of the fiction — naming the UI registry
+a component was copied from, and prose pointing at the repository record. The
+registry pattern caught a fourth site the hand-sweep missed.
+
+## The landing page carries no stat row
+
+**Found 2026-09-04 (design steer #2, pass 9).** `HomeView` receives no billing
+data, so the four cards that filled its `StatsGrid` could only describe the app
+that was rendering them. Deleted rather than rewritten (`57085f8`): a card that
+counts the app is a card the customer cannot read, and the lede plus the route
+cards already do the page's job. `appName` went with it, so
+`routes/index.tsx` no longer passes it. If the landing page ever gets a real
+number — open runs, collected this period — it should come back as a
+`WidgetCard` with a hero, on data this layer actually has.

